add("ScoutGitOpens", "scout", ["operability"], f"""Which files does each census git invocation open, and with which flags? ALLOWED-EXEC: create a synthetic repo under /var/tmp/souji-r18-ScoutGitOpens/ with a tracked file, info/attributes, info/exclude, a work-tree .gitignore and .gitattributes; run under `strace -f -e trace=openat -o …` exactly the git command lines the census uses (copy them from {C}:1000-1135 — rev-parse --is-inside-work-tree, worktree list, the count_unpushed rev-list, ls-files|check-attr, the status line with its -c options) with the census env (GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null GIT_CONFIG_SYSTEM=/dev/null GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0 GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1); report per command which of those files are opened, with O_NONBLOCK or not, and whether status opens info/attributes only when it must compare content (touched file). Install strace only via an allowed non-pacman channel if missing, or report.""")

add("ScoutWorktreeFifo", "scout", ["operability"], f"""Is there a STATIC (no race) census hang? ALLOWED-EXEC: under /var/tmp/souji-r18-ScoutWorktreeFifo/ build a root with repos a, b, c (one tracked file each); in b put a FIFO at the work-tree `.gitignore` (case 1), then `.gitattributes` (case 2), then a nested dir's `.gitignore` (case 3), then `.git/info/exclude` replaced AFTER creation by nothing special (control); run `timeout -k 2 20 bash <base census> --root <root>` where the base census is `git -C {LANE} show {BASE}:tools/souji-census.sh > /var/tmp/souji-r18-ScoutWorktreeFifo/census.sh`, with HOME pointed at an empty /var/tmp dir; record rc, rows, stderr and leftover processes (kill only yours). This tells L1 whether the C1 bug is a race only or also a static hang.""")

add("ScoutSetM", "scout", ["operability"], f"""Bash 5.3 semantics for the C1 watchdog. ALLOWED-EXEC: small scripts under /var/tmp/souji-r18-ScoutSetM/, run with `bash script </dev/null` and also through python subprocess with stdin/stdout pipes and no tty, `set -euo pipefail`: (1) `set -m; f & pid=$!; set +m` — is the job its own process group (`ps -o pgid`), any stderr warning; (2) `kill -TERM -- -$pid` kills a git child blocked opening a FIFO; `wait $pid` rc (143?) and SIGKILL rc (137); (3) does an EXIT trap set in the parent run in the background subshell; (4) `$(…)` capture of the parent finishes while a watchdog `(sleep 30; …) >/dev/null 2>&1 &` is still sleeping, and after `kill $wpid` is its sleep child left behind?; (5) `set -e` interaction with `wait` returning nonzero. Report exact outputs.""")

add("ScoutPyTimeoutLeak", "scout", ["operability"], f"""Static: list every subprocess call in {LANE}/tests/fixtures/r15-census-config.py, r17-census-hygiene.py, r14-census-boundary.py, r15-preservation-evidence.py, r14-evidence-cache.py, r16-landing-gate.py and {LANE}/census/round-17/run-matrix.py: line, timeout value, start_new_session or not, what happens to grandchildren on TimeoutExpired, and whether a census/git grandchild can block on a FIFO. Then match against the leaked processes in {LANE}/census/round-18/leaked-procs-before-1631.txt (which fixture/call produced `r-inc-fifo rev-parse` and `d2-fifo/b … status`). Reads of those named files only.""")

add("ScoutBashFixtureTimeouts", "scout", ["operability"], f"""Static: in {LANE}/tests/fixtures/r12-maintenance-guard.sh, r13-quarantine-bounds.sh, r13-repo-structure.sh, r17-jj-receipts.sh and {LANE}/tools/souji-quarantine.sh, souji-verify.sh, souji-vault-verify.sh, list every `timeout` invocation (flags, whether --foreground, -k) and every background job; GNU timeout without --foreground signals its process group, so say per site whether a blocked grandchild can survive. Reads of those named files only.""")

add("ScoutLeakedProcs", "scout", ["coverage"], f"""Read-only host census of process residue (C3 premise and adjacency). Using `ps -eo pid,ppid,pgid,sid,uid,etimes,stat,wchan:20,args` and /proc/<pid>/cwd links only (never environ, never signal), list every process whose argv or cwd names a /var/tmp, /tmp or /dev/shm path that no longer exists; group by top-level scratch dir family (r15-census-config.*, r17-census-hygiene.*, other lanes' prefixes …), with counts, age range, wchan, parent. Name which families belong to souji fixtures (cross-check fixture tempdir prefixes in {LANE}/tests/fixtures/) and which belong to other lanes or tools (report them for adjacency, never act). Compare with {LANE}/census/round-18/leaked-procs-before-1631.txt.""")

for nm, url, what in [
    ("SrcBashJobControl", "https://www.gnu.org/software/bash/manual/html_node/Job-Control-Basics.html", "that with job control each pipeline/background job runs in its own process group (and what `set -m` enables, from https://www.gnu.org/software/bash/manual/html_node/The-Set-Builtin.html)"),
    ("SrcKill2", "https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/kill.2.html", "that a negative pid signals every process in process group -pid"),
    ("SrcPySubprocess", "https://docs.python.org/3/library/subprocess.html", "what Popen.communicate(timeout)/run(timeout) does to the child on expiry and what start_new_session does (plus os.killpg in https://docs.python.org/3/library/os.html)"),
    ("SrcProcCwd", "https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man5/proc_pid_cwd.5.html", "the cwd symbolic link and the ' (deleted)' annotation for unlinked targets (check proc_pid_exe.5 / proc_pid_fd.5 if the wording lives there)"),
    ("SrcFifoOpenNonblock", "https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/open.2.html", "ENXIO for O_WRONLY|O_NONBLOCK on a FIFO with no reader (the no-reader check C1 fixtures use)"),
    ("SrcCoreutilsTimeout", "https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/html_node/timeout-invocation.html", "the --foreground caveat that children of COMMAND are not timed out (i.e. without it the signal reaches the group); compare with existing row S038 in {LANE}/corpus/SOURCES.md"),
    ("SrcGitAttrC", "https://github.com/git/git/blob/v2.56.0/attr.c", "how git opens $GIT_DIR/info/attributes and .gitattributes (open_nofollow? fopen? any S_ISREG/fstat or size check, any O_NONBLOCK) — the reason a FIFO there blocks; cite file@tag:line"),
    ("SrcGitLsTree", "https://git-scm.com/docs/git-ls-tree", "how `git ls-tree -r --name-only <rev>` lists paths (and `git cat-file -e <rev>:<path>` from https://git-scm.com/docs/git-cat-file) — the pointer-resolution primitive for LG-DANGLING-PTR"),
    ("SrcProcStat", "https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man5/proc_pid_stat.5.html", "starttime field units (clock ticks since boot) and the pgrp/session fields used by the proc census"),
]:
    add(nm, "scout", ["operability" if nm not in ("SrcGitLsTree",) else "calibration"], f"""Source item (frontier step). Open {url} now (record the exact URL fetched, access date 2026-10-20, version/last-updated line if served) and extract {what}. Return one draft SOURCES.md row in the shape of {LANE}/corpus/SOURCES.md (read its header and rows S051–S063 for the column contract) with a verbatim located quote of ≤25 words (section/anchor, `wc -w` count), what it teaches for souji r18, and what it does NOT establish. Never paraphrase inside the quote.""")

